 {:name "kadec-klee-via-norm-sub-square-and-sqrt"
  :level :strategy
  :status :draft
  :maturity :one-shot-heuristic
  :body
  {:problem-class
   "Prove strong convergence in a real Hilbert space from weak convergence together with convergence of norms."
   :proof-shape
   ["Specialize weak convergence at the proposed limit x to obtain `⟪h n, x⟫_ℝ → ⟪x, x⟫_ℝ = ‖x‖²`."
    "Use norm convergence and `Tendsto.pow` to obtain `‖h n‖² → ‖x‖²`."
    "Rewrite `‖h n - x‖²` with the Hilbert-space norm-subtraction identity."
    "Limit arithmetic makes the rewritten expression converge to `‖x‖² - 2‖x‖² + ‖x‖² = 0`."
    "Compose with continuity of the real square root and rewrite `sqrt (‖h n - x‖²) = ‖h n - x‖` using nonnegativity of the norm."]
   :why-this-shape
   "Weak convergence controls the mixed inner-product term, while norm convergence controls the remaining quadratic term. The squared norm is therefore the common expression on which both hypotheses act directly."
   :key-api
   ["norm_sub_sq_real"
    "real_inner_self_eq_norm_sq"
    "Tendsto.pow"
    "Real.continuous_sqrt"
    "Real.sqrt_sq"]
   :boundary
   "This proves the real-Hilbert-space Kadec-Klee implication. It does not by itself establish the separate weak lower-semicontinuity liminf statement."}
