   "Turn weak and norm convergence into convergence of distances in a real inner-product space, including the final conversion from squared distance to distance."
   :api-chain
   [{:lemma "`norm_sub_sq_real`"
     :role
     "Rewrite `‖a-b‖²` exactly as `‖a‖² - 2 * ⟪a,b⟫_ℝ + ‖b‖²`, avoiding a manual inner-product expansion."}
    {:lemma "`real_inner_self_eq_norm_sq`"
     :role
     "Normalize the weak-limit target `⟪x,x⟫_ℝ` to `‖x‖²`."}
    {:lemma "`Real.continuous_sqrt`"
     :role
     "Compose `‖h n-x‖² → 0` with square-root continuity."}
    {:lemma "`Real.sqrt_sq`"
     :role
     "Rewrite `sqrt (‖h n-x‖²)` to `‖h n-x‖`, using `norm_nonneg`."}]
   :use
   "Transport the limit across `norm_sub_sq_real` with `Tendsto.congr`; after limit arithmetic reaches zero, apply `Real.continuous_sqrt.tendsto 0`, compose, rewrite `Real.sqrt_zero`, and use `Real.sqrt_sq (norm_nonneg _)` pointwise."
